eat_baseline\\\",[],\\\"is_reconfigured\\\",\\\"eq\\\",True),\n c(\\\"After the first re-synchronization of both followers each of them still reports six indices of content.\\\",\\\"REPEAT_ROUND1\\\",\\\"repeat_baseline\\\",[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}],\\\"accepted_idx\\\",\\\"eq\\\",6),\n c(\\\"After the second re-synchronization each follower still reports six indices of content.\\\",\\\"REPEAT_ROUND2\\\",\\\"repeat_baseline\\\",[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}],\\\"accepted_idx\\\",\\\"eq\\\",6),\n c(\\\"After the third re-synchronization each follower still reports six indices of content.\\\",\\\"REPEAT_ROUND3\\\",\\\"repeat_baseline\\\",[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}],\\\"accepted_idx\\\",\\\"eq\\\",6),\n c(\\\"After the third re-synchronization a follower's decided log read from index 0 still has six elements.\\\",\\\"REPEAT_ROUND3\\\",\\\"repeat_baseline\\\",[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"ne\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}],\\\"suffix_entries\\\",\\\"eq\\\",6),\n c(\\\"After the third re-synchronization the leader still reports six decided indices.\\\",\\\"REPEAT_ROUND3\\\",\\\"repeat_baseline\\\",[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}],\\\"decided_idx\\\",\\\"eq\\\",6),\n c(\\\"After the third re-synchronization the leader's decided index is still covered by the entries it holds.\\\",\\\"REPEAT_ROUND3\\\",\\\"repeat_baseline\\\",[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}],\\\"decided_eq_accepted\\\",\\\"eq\\\",True),\n]\nexp={\\\"investigation_id\\\":QC,\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"omnipaxos/tests/assurance_generated.rs\\\",\\\"files\\\":{},\n \\\"previous_id\\\":EXPR,\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"Adds a repeated-resynchronization case that performs three rounds of two-follower reconnection after a decided StopSign and samples every round, to test whether the reported index inflation compounds rather than being a one-off shift.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"sync_log_accounting\\\",\\\"create_log_sync\\\",\\\"send_accsync_valid_entries\\\",\\\"handle_promise_accept_resync\\\",\\\"handle_accepted_decision\\\",\\\"is_reconfigured_endpoint\\\",\\\"internal_get_entry_type\\\",\\\"read_decided_suffix_public\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Seven cases in one execution over three real OmniPaxos instances in one process with MemoryStorage and a deterministic FIFO in-process network: the previously fixed resync, single, control, newterm, snap and the new repeated-resynchronization case, which repeats the two-follower reconnection three times and samples all three nodes after each round under REPEAT_BASELINE/REPEAT_ROUND1..3. Public API only.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Entry type Value has Snapshot = NoSnapshot; ClusterConfig { configuration_id: 1, nodes: [1,2,3], flexible_quorum: None } with default ServerConfig (batch_size 1).\\\",\\\"Each round repeats the same public calls: node 1 and node 2 call reconnected(3) and the FIFO queue is drained to quiet, so every round is an independent re-established-connection event.\\\",\\\"Leadership stays with node 3 throughout; no tick() timers run.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Snapshots, trimming, compaction and batching are not exercised.\\\",\\\"No crate or package test suite is executed; only the generated test file.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":3,\\\"entries_before_stopsign\\\":5,\\\"rounds\\\":3}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Same prefix as the fixed experiments of this lineage (node 3 leads via try_become_leader, five entries appended and decided, a StopSign proposed with reconfigure() and decided), then REPEAT_BASELINE samples all three nodes. Three rounds follow; each round calls node1.reconnected(3) and node2.reconnected(3), drains the queue to quiet, and samples all three nodes as REPEAT_ROUND1, REPEAT_ROUND2 and REPEAT_ROUND3. Samples report accepted_idx, decided_idx, decided_eq_accepted, is_reconfigured, read(5), read(6) and read_decided_suffix(0).\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"repeat_baseline\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"REPEAT_BASELINE\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[]},{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"round1\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"REPEAT_ROUND1\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[]},{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"round2\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"REPEAT_ROUND2\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[]},{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"round3\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"REPEAT_ROUND3\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":comps,\n \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"Adds the repeated-resynchronization case; the previously generated cases are unchanged apart from sharing the same execution.\\\",\\\"No production code was modified.\\\"]}\nup={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Test whether the witnessed inflation compounds. The inflation adds one index per re-synchronization of a replica whose resume point already covers its StopSign, and the leader's phantom decision follows the inflated reports, so repeated re-established-connection events predict a reported accepted and decided index that keeps growing while the content stays at six indices. The submitted successor repeats the two-follower reconnection three times in the same run and samples all three nodes after each round, with comparisons requiring the baseline (six indices, StopSign decided) and, after every round, that re-synchronized replicas still report at most the six indices they hold, that their decided-log read still has six elements, and that the leader still reports six decided indices covered by its entries.\\\"),\n \\\"experiment\\\":exp}\njson.dump(up, open('update.json','w'), indent=1); print('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -c 900\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
